# ── Secrets / local config ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.template
*.key
*.pem

# GCP credentials for VOD reprocessing (see REPROCESS_VOD.md)
.gcp-adc.json
.gcp-*.json
gcp-*.json

# ── Per-deployment runtime state ─────────────────────────────────────────
# These files are seeded empty in the repo; the app writes user data into
# them at runtime. Don't track those edits.
outputs.json
vod-jobs.json
# rules.json is the live word rules, edited from the Rules tab. The tracked
# starter is rules.starter.json; the server copies it to rules.json on first
# run, so an update never overwrites a hall's own rules.
rules.json
# The overlay gate's hall settings. overlay-gate.example.json is the tracked
# list of keys and defaults; a hall's own copy is its own.
overlay-gate.json
# glossary.json is TRACKED again as of 2026-09-01. It was ignored while this
# project's repo was public, because the file names the event. The development
# repo went private that day, which removed the reason there; the mandir repo
# is public and tracks it too, because what the file holds is a katha's
# vocabulary and nothing private (no keys, no names of people). Tracking it is
# the point: the glossary is the whole quality margin (a briefed model scores
# 24/24 on terminology, the same model cold scores like the cheap one), it was
# surviving only as an untracked file on one Windows PC, and it is the artefact
# a Gujarati reader reviews. An unbacked-up file that nobody can review is the
# bigger risk.
# glossary.example.json stays as the empty schema for a fresh deployment.
#
# Still true, and unchanged by any of this: NO KEYS IN TRACKED FILES. Private
# is not a reason to relax .env, and a public repo is a reason to be stricter.

# Operator logs. A deployment that redirects server output into the repo
# leaves `?? logs/` in git status — the same invisible trap as the
# glossary, and the mandir PC walked into it within the hour. A caption
# log holds the whole katha transcript, so committing one to a public
# repo is worse than the glossary would have been.
logs/
*.log

# ── Generated / cached / large ───────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Frontend
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Local artefacts (recordings, uploads, samples) ───────────────────────
results/
uploads/
samples/
screenshots/
# (samples/ also gitignored — drop your own test audio in there locally.)

# ── Media (test clips, intermediates) ────────────────────────────────────
*.mov
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.wav
*.mp3
*.flac
*.m4a

